# -*- mode:org; coding:utf-8 -*-
#+TITLE: alfe-cad-nil-catch-all-message -- on AutoCAD a caught error can have a NIL message; alfe's CAD side then reports a failed request as OK or fails in its own error path
#+STATUS: DONE
#+PRIORITY: P2
#+TYPE: bug
#+DATE: 2026-10-23

* Symptom
AutoCAD 2022 returns NIL from (vl-catch-all-error-message e) for some
caught errors -- measured for vl-exit-with-error / vl-exit-with-value
outside a VLX (control-flow probe, jobs 17398575920 / 17398575921;
BricsCAD answers ""). alfe's CAD-side code assumes the message is a
string:

- the emitted request evaluator (autolisp-front-end/source/file-protocol.lisp,
  AUTOLISP-EVAL-REQUEST-SOURCE): (setq alfe--err (vl-catch-all-error-message
  alfe--err)) then (if err (autolisp-raise err) r) -- a NIL message makes
  the FAILED request report DONE OK (a false success);
- autolisp-front-end/source/runtime/autolisp-bootstrap.lsp:
  (autolisp-raise (vl-catch-all-error-message ...)), (strcat "ERROR ..."
  (vl-catch-all-error-message ...)) and the form-read / eval paths;
  autolisp-front-end/source/runtime/autolisp-remote-io.lsp likewise -- a
  NIL there makes strcat or the raise fail inside the error handling.

* Fix (requested)
One CAD-side helper -- (alfe-catch-all-message e) => the message, or a
fixed text when it is NIL or "" -- used at every such site
(autolisp-bootstrap-render-error already did this for the bootstrap's
fatal path).

* Fix (2026-10-23)
- autolisp-bootstrap.lsp defines (alfe-catch-all-message E): the
  message of the caught error E when it is a non-empty string, else the
  fixed text "the engine supplied no message". That is the text
  autolisp-raise already put in the error context for an empty message,
  and one autolisp-vague-error-message-p recognises, so a failed request
  still gets its form appended on stderr. Pure ASCII, fixed arity, no
  ERROR.
- "" is mapped to the fixed text as well. On BricsCAD this changes
  nothing on the request paths (autolisp-raise and
  autolisp-request-failure-text already turned "" into that text); it
  only makes the log lines ("ERROR eval ...: ", "WARN log-setup: ",
  "ERROR protocol read: ") and the source-load diagnostic readable
  instead of ending in an empty message.
- The bootstrap is the first file loaded on the CAD, but run-common.lsp
  reports a failed bootstrap LOAD before (or without) it, so the
  emitted run-common.lsp defines the same function right after
  alfe-debug-log.
- Sites routed through the helper:
  - file-protocol.lisp (emitted run-common.lsp): the bootstrap-LOAD and
    runtime-LOAD failure logs, autolisp-eval-request-source (the false
    success), the server-loop catch (*ALFE-LOOP-ERRMSG*, used in strcat);
  - autolisp-bootstrap.lsp: autolisp-source-load's re-raise, the
    form-read and form-eval source-raise paths, alfe-load /
    alfe-load-onfailure re-raise, the log-setup WARN, the REPL loop's
    read and eval ERROR lines; autolisp-bootstrap-render-error now also
    rejects a NIL / "" message (it returned NIL to a strcat);
  - autolisp-remote-io.lsp: the "ERROR protocol read" line and the
    request-failure text.
  The two autolisp-quit-signal-p tests keep the raw message: that
  predicate already accepts NIL, and must not see a substituted text.
- Tests (autolisp-front-end/tests/file-protocol-tests.lisp, hosted
  clautolisp with vl-catch-all-error-message redefined to answer NIL as
  AutoCAD does): PROTOCOL-NIL-CATCH-ALL-MESSAGE-REQUEST-FAILS ("(/ 1 0)"
  reports FAIL with the fixed text) and
  PROTOCOL-NIL-CATCH-ALL-MESSAGE-LOAD-FAILS (a failing form in a loaded
  file FAILs the load and stops it). Both were red before the fix (every
  request reported DONE OK).

* Vendor check (pending)
On AutoCAD: alfe -x of a vl-exit form, e.g.
(vl-exit-with-error "x"), must report FAIL (with "the engine supplied
no message" and the form on stderr), not DONE OK.

* Vendor check (2026-10-24) -- DONE

verify:autocad-nil-catch-all:windows (MR !481, job 17437581678), alfe -x
'(vl-exit-with-error (vl-symbol-name (quote NILCATCH)))' on AutoCAD 2022:

- --mode automation (the GUI): "ERROR protocol request 1: the engine
  supplied no message [form: (VL-EXIT-WITH-ERROR ...)]", alfe exit 1;
- --mode batch (AcCoreConsole): the same line, exit 1.

The failed request is reported as FAIL with the fixed text and the form, not
DONE OK, on both AutoCAD engines. The job stays (manual) as the regression
check.
